This file travels with the two rnplens artefacts: it is named in pyproject's
license-files, so the wheel carries it as rnplens-0.4.0.dev0.dist-info/licenses/NOTICE,
and in MANIFEST.in, so the sdist carries it at the archive root. It is deliberately NOT
shipped with rnplens-assistant, which bundles no third-party code of any kind; Part 0
states, entry by entry, which licence actually obliges a notice to travel.

This NOTICE aggregates the third-party attributions that the RNPLens distributions are
obliged to carry. It is a factual record of what the files and their upstream licence
texts state. It is not legal advice and expresses no opinion on whether any licence
combination is permissible. Items whose permission is not established are listed in
Part E and are marked UNRESOLVED rather than asserted.

RNPLens itself is covered by the MIT LICENSE at the repository root, and
rnplens-assistant by the byte-identical copy at assistant/LICENSE. Attribution for
first-party code rests entirely on those files: no source file in the repository carries a
licence header or an SPDX-License-Identifier.

Two distributions are built from this tree:
  * rnplens 0.4.0.dev0            — wheel and sdist
  * rnplens-assistant 0.1.0.dev0  — wheel and sdist
